I'm about to change these lists to use VERP on outgoing mail --
including the recipient's address in the reverse-path of each mail to
make it easier to track bounces. 

Since the most reliable way to filter list mail is by its reverse-path,
I figured I ought to give a little bit of notice of the change -- so if
you were filtering on the reverse-path
'linux-XXX-bounces@lists.infradead.org' you will now need to match
'linux-XXX-bounces.*@lists.infradead.org' instead, if in fact you're not
already doing so.

